.1016/0377-2217(78)90138-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>&#x000c2;anker</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Charnes</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Some models for estimating technical and scale inefficiencies in Data Envelopment Analysis</article-title><source>Manag Sci</source><year>1984</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>1078</fpage><lpage>1092</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Banker</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Estimating the most productive scale size using Data Envelopment Analysis</article-title><source>Eur J Oper Res</source><year>1984</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>34</fpage><lpage>44</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0377-2217(84)90006-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>WW</given-names></name><name><surname>Seiford</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Thanassoulis</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Zanakis</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DEA and its use in different countries</article-title><source>Eur J Oper Res</source><year>2004</year><volume>154</volume><fpage>337</fpage><lpage>344</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0377-2217(03)00173-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bowlin</surname><given-names>WF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Measuring performance: An introduction to data envelopment analysis (DEA)</article-title><source>J Cost Anal</source><year>1998</